From b9c5efe615c0434a51b3336cf3746d37b795d2e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nrvate <11264848+nrvate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:20:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] The functions that observe from geopos give the caller's
 observer back; the Earth and SE_ECL_NUT are no body to rise, phase or be
 occulted (UPSTREAM-BUGS 291, 292, 293, G180, G24)

What was wrong (291): every function that observes from geopos set it as
the context's observer (set_topo_for_this_call(), SWI_CFG_LOCAL, so
published to no other context) and left it there. At UT 2433282.5, Swiss
files, a context with swe_set_topo(-70, -30, 0): the topocentric Moon
61.9355771 before, 60.8485787 (Zurich's) after swe_rise_trans() (every
path), swe_rise_trans_true_hor(), swe_sol_eclipse_how(), _when_loc(),
swe_lun_occult_when_loc(), swe_lun_eclipse_how(), _when_loc(),
swe_gauquelin_sector() methods 2-5, swe_vis_limit_mag(),
swe_heliacal_pheno_ut() and swe_heliacal_ut() at Zurich; 60.8732 after
swe_sol_eclipse_where() (the central line's), 61.1414 after _when_glob(),
61.4540 after swe_lun_occult_where(). With no observer set the next
topocentric call answered where a fresh context refuses. The default
context the same. 18 of G180's 24 calls.

What was wrong (292): swe_rise_trans() and _true_hor() answered the
Earth, the rise 2433282.5833 and upper transit 2433283.1964 of
swe_calc()'s geocentric zero vector; swe_pheno() and _ut() OK with the
apparent diameter 180 deg; swe_lun_occult_where() 9 (central, annular) at
138.38 E 24.28 S; _when_glob() and _when_loc() refused it with the
search's "jd nan outside the range ..." (the upstream build's _when_glob()
on Moshier does not end). swetest -pC -rise printed a rise at 02:00.

What was wrong (293): SE_ECL_NUT was taken for a body: swe_rise_trans()
rise 2433282.9310, transit 2433283.2613; swe_gauquelin_sector() 16.6929
(method 0), 17.8208 (1), 16.4906 (2), methods 4 and 5 through
pla_diam[-1], an out-of-bounds read (16.490590 here, 16.542019 on another
build); swe_calc_pctr() 41.8330 -16.3419 33.1551 AU from the Sun, Mars
from it 218.9725; swe_helio_cross() and _ut() a search that had not ended
after 300 s (first step to JD 5.3e8). The occultation functions set every
negative number without a star to the Sun (_when_glob() 2433359.147).
pla_diam[] and mag_elem[] were bounded above only at every read.

Fix: behind #ifndef SWE_UPSTREAM_COMPAT, the 12 public wrappers that reach
set_topo_for_this_call() (swecl.c: swe_rise_trans_r, _true_hor_r,
swe_sol_eclipse_how_r, _when_loc_r, _where_r, _when_glob_r,
swe_lun_occult_when_loc_r, _where_r, swe_lun_eclipse_how_r; swehel.c:
swe_vis_limit_mag_r, swe_heliacal_pheno_ut_r, swe_heliacal_ut_r) capture
the configuration after the hold's sync and give the observer group back
at return (caller_site_back(): swi_config_apply(SWI_CFG_TOPO) under
SWI_CFG_LOCAL, bug 273's mechanism: nothing published, nothing claimed,
the cached site dropped only if it moved). Nested calls give back the
outer call's geopos, so the outer searches run as before; every call's
answers are bit for bit the tip's whatever the caller's observer (24
calls x unset/geopos/far x twice). no_body_seen() refuses SE_EARTH and
every negative number (not a star asked with one) in
swe_rise_trans_true_hor_r_body (so swe_rise_trans), swe_pheno (the Earth;
negatives it refused already), swe_gauquelin_sector (negatives; the Earth
since 274), the three occultation bodies (before upstream's "ipl < 0 ->
0", which the star's case keeps); swe_helio_cross()/_ut() add ipl < SE_SUN
to their refused objects; swe_calc_pctr() refuses a negative body or
centre: ERR, outputs 0 (bug 239), a message. In both builds (memory
safety) every pla_diam[] and mag_elem[] read is bounded below too (ipl >=
0): eclipse_where, eclipse_how, occult_when_glob, occult_when_loc,
swe_pheno, swe_rise_trans_true_hor, get_sun_rad_plus_refr; the compat
preprocessed sources differ from the tip's in those 8 conditions only.
Cost: 2000 swe_rise_trans() Moon rises 2.15169e9 -> 2.15308e9
instructions (+0.06 %) unset, +0.09 % with the observer elsewhere; no hot
path.

Gate G180 tests/sitebody.c (new): (a) after each of 24 calls at Zurich
on explicit contexts unset and at 70W 30S, the topocentric Moon, Mars,
Spica with speeds (1950, J2000, Swiss and Moshier) as before and as a
fresh context's, 24; (b) each call's answers the same whatever the
caller's observer, 24; (c) the default context unset and at 70W 30S, and
a context made after, 3; (d) the Earth refused in rise and set, the
phenomena and the occultations on three ephemerides, a star with its
number the star, the Earth where it has a place answered, 10; (e) -1, -2,
-100, -2147483647 refused there and in the sectors, the crossings (in
alarmed children) and swe_calc_pctr(), a star with ipl -1 the star, the
Sun and Cupido answered, 21. After 0 of 82 fail; before (ts20 tip) 42 (18
a, 2 c, 7 d, 15 e); the upstream build 45 (those, b's Gauquelin method 0
topocentric of bug 273, e's swe_pheno() and _ut()). G24 site_left_moved:
0 shipped, 1.087 deg compat; earth_body_answered: 0/4 shipped, 4/4
compat; eclnut_body_answered: 0/5 shipped, 5/5 compat. G175, G167, G174,
G134, G161, G82, G106, G124, G160, G121, G109, G164, G20, G120, G81,
cfgleak and G24 pass.

Files: swecl.c, swehel.c, sweph.c, sweph.h, tests/sitebody.c,
tests/Makefile, tests/compat.c, notes/UPSTREAM-BUGS.md, notes/REVIEW.md.
