+/* sitebody.c -- G180: the functions that observe from geopos give the
+ * caller's observer back, and those that take a body refuse the Earth and
+ * the numbers that are no body.
+ *
+ * The defect (UPSTREAM-BUGS 291): the functions that observe from geopos
+ * set it as the context's observer (swe_set_topo() for that call alone,
+ * published to no other context) and left it there: after
+ * swe_rise_trans() (every path), swe_rise_trans_true_hor(),
+ * swe_sol_eclipse_how(), _when_loc(), _where(), _when_glob(),
+ * swe_lun_occult_when_loc(), _where(), swe_lun_eclipse_how(), _when_loc(),
+ * swe_gauquelin_sector() methods 2 to 5, swe_vis_limit_mag(),
+ * swe_heliacal_pheno_ut() and swe_heliacal_ut() at Zurich, with the
+ * caller's observer at 70 W 30 S, the topocentric Moon at UT 2433282.5
+ * (1950) on the Swiss files was 60.8486 for 61.9356 deg (Zurich's; after
+ * sol_eclipse_where() the central line's, 60.8732; after _when_glob()
+ * 61.1414), and with none set a topocentric call answered where it is
+ * refused ("geographic position has not been set"); 18 of the 24 calls
+ * below.
+ * Check (a): each of 24 calls (those, and as controls
+ * swe_lun_occult_when_glob(), swe_lun_eclipse_when(), Gauquelin method 0
+ * with SEFLG_TOPOCTR, swe_topo_arcus_visionis(), swe_heliacal_angle(),
+ * swe_azalt()) at Zurich (400 m) on an explicit context whose observer is
+ * unset and one at 70 W 30 S: afterwards the topocentric Moon, Mars and
+ * Spica with speeds at 1950 and J2000, Swiss files and Moshier, bit for
+ * bit as before the call and as a fresh context's, or the refusal and its
+ * message: 24 checks. Check (b): each call's own answers (return, times,
+ * attributes, places, message) bit for bit the same with the caller's
+ * observer unset, at Zurich and at 70 W 30 S, called twice: 24. Check (c):
+ * the default context unset (before anything publishes an observer), then
+ * at 70 W 30 S, after the 24 calls as before them and as a fresh
+ * context's; a context made after them inherits the published 70 W 30 S,
+ * not Zurich: 3.
+ *
+ * The defect (UPSTREAM-BUGS 292): swe_rise_trans() and _true_hor()
+ * answered the Earth, the rise and transits of swe_calc()'s geocentric
+ * zero vector (rise 2433282.5833, upper transit 2433283.1964 at 1950,
+ * Zurich); swe_pheno() and swe_pheno_ut() its phenomena, OK with the
+ * apparent diameter 180 deg; swe_lun_occult_where() 9 (central, annular)
+ * at 138.38 E 24.28 S; swe_lun_occult_when_glob() and _when_loc() refused
+ * it with "jd nan outside the range ...".
+ * Check (d): the Earth on the Swiss files, Moshier and de200 in
+ * swe_rise_trans() (rise, set, both transits, Hindu rising, the slow
+ * method), swe_rise_trans_true_hor(), swe_pheno() and _ut() (geocentric,
+ * topocentric), and the three occultation functions (each in a child
+ * process, 10 s: the upstream build's search of the Earth does not end):
+ * ERR, the outputs 0 (filled with 7 before), the message naming the
+ * Earth: 7 checks; a star asked with ipl SE_EARTH the star bit for bit
+ * (swe_rise_trans(), the occultations): 2; the Earth where it has a place
+ * (swe_helio_cross(), swe_calc_pctr() from the Sun, swe_nod_aps()
+ * geocentric and heliocentric) answered: 1.
+ *
+ * The defect (UPSTREAM-BUGS 293): SE_ECL_NUT, swe_calc()'s nutation and
+ * obliquity, answered as a body: swe_rise_trans() rise 2433282.9310,
+ * transit 2433283.2613; swe_gauquelin_sector() 16.6929 (method 0),
+ * 17.8208 (1), 16.4906 (2), its methods 4 and 5 from pla_diam[-1] (read
+ * out of bounds: 16.490590 on one build, 16.542019 on another);
+ * swe_calc_pctr() 41.8330 -16.3419 33.1551 from the Sun, Mars from it
+ * 218.9725; swe_helio_cross() searched without end (300 s); and every
+ * negative number without a star was the Sun in the three occultation
+ * functions (their solar eclipses: when_glob() 2433359.147).
+ * Check (e): -1, -2, -100 and -2147483647 in (d)'s calls, on the same
+ * ephemerides, in swe_gauquelin_sector() (each method), swe_helio_cross()
+ * and _ut() (each in a child process, 20 s) and swe_calc_pctr() (as the
+ * body and as the centre): ERR, the outputs 0, a message: 17 checks; a
+ * star asked with ipl -1 the star bit for bit (swe_rise_trans(),
+ * swe_gauquelin_sector() methods 0 and 4, the occultations): 3; the Sun
+ * in the occultations and Cupido in swe_rise_trans() and
+ * swe_gauquelin_sector() method 4 still answered: 1.
+ *
+ * Measured: after the fix all 82 checks pass, every call's answers bit
+ * for bit the tip's whatever the observer. Before it (ts20 tip) 42 fail:
+ * 18 of (a), 2 of (c) (the default context, unset and at 70 W 30 S), 7
+ * of (d) (the Earth answered; the occultations' NaN message), 15 of (e)
+ * (every function but swe_pheno(), which the fork refused already; the
+ * crossings killed at 20 s). The upstream build fails 45: those, (b)'s
+ * Gauquelin method 0 topocentric (bug 273) and (e)'s swe_pheno() and
